From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:22:07 -0400
Subject: Vulkan: Fix content-defined tracking for 3D images

Unlike every other image type, when content subresources are defined for
3D images are tracked per "slice" rather than layer.  However, many
operations turn the layer range to [0, 1) for them, leading to incorrect
content-defined tracking.  This change modifies the few places that need
it to take 3D images into account and use the z/depth instead of
layer/count for tracking.

This change also paves the way for fixing staged clear of 3D images in
some corner cases.

Bug: chromium:556750158
Change-Id: I5cbc364016b93b03342f672ebbee728e574d5234
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8446121
Commit-Queue: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Charlie Lao <cclao@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Amirali Abdolrashidi <abdolrashidi@google.com>

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): this ANGLE revision predates the
gl::OwnerLevel/OwnerLayer/OwnerImageIndex types, so the fix is expressed
with gl::LevelIndex, uint32_t layers and gl::ImageIndex (adding .get()
where the gl::ImageIndex factories take GLint). The layer-range helpers
(matchesLayerRange/intersectsLayerRange/getDestSubresource) move from
SubresourceUpdate onto ImageHelper exactly as upstream does; their old
SubresourceUpdate declarations are removed, and the remaining caller in
ImageHelper::removeSingleStagedClearAfterInvalidate (already gone
upstream, still present on this revision) is switched to the ImageHelper
helper so the old definition is not left unresolved at link time. New
end2end test expectations are dropped (test-only drift).

